 drive.  aSystem requirements for Windows: i486 or Pentium PC; 8MB RAM or higher; Windows 95, 98, NT 4.0 with Service Pack 3 ; 10MB available hard disk space; CD-ROM drive.  aTitle from disc label.  a"Prepared in cooperation with the Nevada Operations Office, U.S. Department of Energy, under Interagency Agreement DE-AI0897NV12033."  aGeologists.  aThe results of thirteen of the many studies that were undertaken to foster a fuller and more comprehensive understanding of the tectonic environment of Yucca Mountain are presented in this document.  aProduction level cataloging.5DLC 0aGeologyzNevadazYucca Mountain Region. 0aRadioactive waste siteszNevadazYucca Mountain RegionxEvaluation. 0aGroundwater flowzNevadazYucca Mountain Region.2 aGeological Survey (U.S.)02759cmm  22004694a    00038644 DLC20041214112939.0co||||000622s2000    miu    f   m        eng    a   00038644   a0472002791  aDLCcDLCdDLC  ae-uk-en00aZ6605.A56aPR23110a6002131 aVoigts, Linda E.10aScientific and medical writings in Old and Middle Englishh[computer file] :ban electronic reference /cLinda Ehrsam Voigts and Patricia Deery Kurtz.1 iTitle on disc label:aScientific and medical writing in Old and Middle English  aMac/Windows version.  aComputer data and program.  aAnn Arbor :bUniversity of Michigan Press,cc2000.  a1 computer optical disc ;c4 3/4 in. 0aSociety for early English and Norse electronic texts.nSeries B ;v1  aSystem requirements for PC: 486 PC; 8MB RAM; Windows 95, 98, or NT; 256-color monitor (640 x 480 resolution display); quad-speed CD-ROM drive.  aSystem requirements for Macintosh: 68020 processor; 4MB RAM; System 7.1 or higher; 256-color monitor (640 x 480 resolution display); quad-speed CD-ROM drive.  aTitle from title screen.  aEd. statement from disc label.  aOld and Middle English scholars.  aProvides information on more than 8,500 texts from the earliest significant body of technical and learned wr